    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green. The audit log confirms the new behavior: `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` \u2014 the registration date `2026-08-17` (August, on/after 1 July) falls in fiscal year 2027, so both the membership number's year segment and the new `fiscalYear` field (`FY27`) use the fiscal year.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived owner values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, identified by the calendar year it ends in).\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (source of the generated `OwnerDto`):\n- Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`).\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect fiscal-year semantics.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**:\n- Added `@Mapping` for the new `fiscalYear` field.\n- Added `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 the core rule: month \u2265 July \u2192 `year + 1`, else `year`.\n- Added `fiscalYear(owner)` returning `\"FY\" + (fiscalYear % 100)`, or `null` when no registration date.\n- Changed `membershipNumber` to derive its `<YY>` segment from the fiscal year instead of the raw calendar year.\n- Replaced `tenureDays` (365-day windows) with `tenureFiscalYears`, counting elapsed fiscal-year boundaries; `membershipPoints` now awards its 3 points when tenure exceeds one elapsed fiscal year.\n\nEverything derives from the stored `registrationDate`, which the controller already writes business-day-adjusted, so the fiscal year, membership number, and tenure all use the adjusted date. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: the fiscal-year label uses the ending-year convention (a July 2026 date \u2192 `FY27`), since the spec fixes the `FY<YY>` format but not which boundary year names it; the AU-themed data (postcodes, phone format) makes the ending-year financial-year convention the natural fit.",
